const extraCases={"market":[["A trader calls a recent factory stoppage proof that tomorrow’s bid will rise. What would you distinguish?","A reported stoppage, available stock and a guaranteed future quote are three different claims.","Ask which receiving users are affected before deciding every unit has the same urgency.","A captain may wait with owned cargo, but should know the storage, time and uncertain sale price."],["A mixed shipment has one disputed seal. Should every crate be rejected?","Trace the disputed lot separately; a shared departure does not establish identical condition.","Hear the handlers before assigning the whole delay to the receiving crew.","The buyer can decline an uncertain lot without taking ownership of unrelated client cargo."],["A familiar supplier asks you to omit the last receiving defect from a certificate. What matters?","Keep the defect and its repair in the condition record. Familiarity cannot verify missing work.","Give the supplier room to explain the repair without making the buyer carry an undisclosed risk.","Both parties need the material facts before choosing their terms."]],"contracts":[["Two goods in one delivery have different receiving needs. What should the promise contain?","Identify each product, quantity and receiving condition; a combined total can hide the missing line.","Ask which receiving crew can handle the whole shipment without leaving one lot unattended.","Accept only a handover the assigned holds and timetable can actually support."],["A detour would help one client and make another delivery late. Whose clock matters?","Check both signed deadlines against the actual route. A worthy purpose does not alter an existing contract.","Explain the conflict before treating one waiting crew as an invisible cost.","The captain chooses the route with the stated breach consequences still attached."],["A client calls a lost shipment theft. What would you ask for?","Compare the actual loss and custody record before assigning intent.","The affected client deserves an account, and the surviving crew deserves a hearing.","An honest account does not erase liability; liability does not establish deliberate theft."]],"shipyard":[["A repair works on the flagship but fails on an escort. Would you repeat the fitting?","Compare the actual hull, interfaces and loaded conditions before copying the result.","Ask the escort’s engineer what happened at the moment of failure.","A crew can choose further work only after its limits and cost are clear."],["A tank upgrade leaves a captain expecting more propellant already aboard. What should be checked?","Separate capacity, actual fuel and the mass used in the flight plan.","Explain the difference before a departure queue turns confusion into blame.","The captain chooses how much to load; an empty tank upgrade is not a fuel purchase."],["A tired crew asks for the fastest possible repair sign-off. Where would you pause?","Keep the critical operating test even when cosmetic work can wait.","Fatigue is a reason to help the crew arrange time, not to hide a missing inspection.","Offer the safe available options and let the captain choose with their actual limits visible."]],"fleet":[["A sold ship returns to the local register with its upgrades. What should the next buyer see?","The hull identity, condition and fitted equipment must follow the actual vessel.","A former owner may care about the ship’s history without retaining a claim over the new sale.","Buying it back is a new purchase at the posted full value, not a reversal of the discounted sale."],["A captain changes flagship before a specialist handover. What needs another look?","Match the assignment to the reserved hull, not just the captain’s new command vessel.","Ask the receiving crew whether the originally assigned stores and people are still coming.","A flagship change is the captain’s decision; it does not transfer every signed duty automatically."],["An overdue berthed vessel may be auctioned. What should the record distinguish?","Identify the local credit obligation, sale proceeds and remaining balance separately.","An owner needs to know which vessel is affected before an ordinary berth becomes a surprise loss.","A forced sale does not make the remaining fleet free of any surviving obligation."]],"security":[["A liberated station still appears in a report about a nearby route. Is the circular wrong?","A recorded liberation clears that blockade; it does not verify every later approach.","Receiving crews need both the good news and the remaining uncertainty.","A captain can travel with the current warning rather than a promise of permanent safety."],["A witness asks for confidentiality while another office needs corroboration. What can survive both needs?","Separate the attributable observation from identifying details that need restricted custody.","Explain the limits of confidentiality before asking the witness to trust the receiving desk.","The witness should understand what may be shared; confidentiality is not permission to invent evidence."],["A confident bounty lead is old. What would make it useful now?","Keep its date and seek an independent recent observation.","Do not turn the crew that repeated it into the person who originally saw the target.","The captain decides whether to investigate; an accepted warrant does not guarantee an encounter."]],"relay":[["An escort reaches the destination but its client’s acknowledgement is missing. What would you report?","Arrival, protection and the receiving acknowledgement are separate observations.","Ask the receiving coordinator what the client actually confirmed.","A captain should see the unresolved handover before assuming the assignment is settled."],["A passenger wants a private destination change during a medical transfer. What would you separate?","Check the existing manifest, receiving facility and the authority attached to any change.","Hear the traveller without treating their medical needs as ordinary freight instructions.","An informed request matters, but it does not silently rewrite another person’s consent or the signed charter."],["A departure briefing describes a different route from the one now plotted. What is the next step?","Match the quoted briefing to its origin, destination and validity period.","Tell the crew which part of the old preparation remains useful.","Replanning belongs to the captain; the wrong briefing must not be presented as current coverage."]],"clinic":[["A reserve donor wants to know who used the supplies. What can you explain?","Confirm the receiving and reserve records without inventing a patient-level account.","Appreciate the contribution while protecting the people who needed care.","Giving supplies does not buy access to someone else’s medical history."],["A supervised study would overlap a freight deadline. Who should decide?","Show the actual service days beside the signed delivery deadline.","Ask whether the crew can participate without making consent feel compulsory.","The captain may decline the study; participation does not pause other obligations."],["A crew is ready to work but one specialist remains off duty. Is that a contradiction?","Collective readiness and an individual duty assignment describe different things.","Ask the specialist what their preparation requires without inventing an injury.","The captain controls the assignment within the agreed duty limits and continuing wages."]],"local":[["A rumour repeats a captain’s failure but omits the later repair. How would you retell it?","Keep the original breach and the dated corrective action together.","Give the affected people room to describe what repair meant to them.","A new action can change a relationship without erasing the old record."],["A discreet tenant offers more rent for privacy. What should the host make clear?","Identify the goods, custody, concealment and actual seizure liability.","Do not make a warehouse owner discover the risk after the tenant has left.","The owner can refuse; a friendly introduction is not acceptance of a lease."],["An old friend asks for a recommendation you cannot yet support. What is an honest answer?","Name the kept promise you can verify, and the parts you cannot.","Explain the limit without pretending the friendship means nothing.","A person may remain welcome even when you will not put your name behind a professional claim."]],"bank":[["Rates are rising more slowly than before. Is that the same as rates falling?","Separate the level, direction and pace of the change.","Ask which distinction matters to the captain’s actual journey.","Fixing is a new quoted agreement; a slower rise does not alter an old fixed loan."],["A captain has deposits at another station but an obligation here. What would you clarify?","Distinguish local funds, network holdings and the loan held by this branch.","Explain why the receiving desk cannot call every distant reserve ready cash here.","The captain chooses the transfer and repayment plan with each branch’s terms intact."],["A fleet valuation is high while available cash is low. What is the missing question?","Ask which assets can meet the obligation and when, rather than counting estimates as cash.","A forced sale affects a crew and deserves a clear account of the remaining balance.","Owning valuable hulls does not make a new borrowing decision risk-free."]],"authority":[["A treaty argument is used to claim exemption from a local clearance. What would you distinguish?","Representation and a hearing do not issue a destination licence.","Provide the proper receiving authority and interpreter where required.","A person can challenge a rule through the recognised process without pretending it has already been waived."],["A liberated station wants a fast recovery handover. What remains necessary?","Match the manifest and receiving responsibility to the actual supplies.","Include the receiving residents in the recovery plan rather than speaking for all of them.","Urgency does not give one liaison permission to consent for every affected person."],["A specimen changes owners but its custodians dispute the allowed study. What record matters?","Examine the actual transfer and consent conditions for that collection.","Hear the custodians without assuming every member of their community agrees.","Buying a specimen does not buy unrestricted access to the people and history attached to it."]],"warehouse":[["A tenant’s goods remain in a bay after the owner needs space. Can the owner sell them?","The ownership and reserved term remain distinct from who owns the warehouse.","Contact the receiving tenant before treating their delay as abandonment.","The owner can plan later capacity, but cannot collect or sell the client lot as personal inventory."],["Concealment has been depleted before a restricted tenant’s next inspection. What should be recorded?","Identify the actual matching packages still stored here and which inspection used one.","The owner needs the changed protection explained before assuming the earlier arrangement remains ready.","Concealment changes detection risk; it never guarantees clearance or transfers away liability."],["Two stations use the same abbreviated bay label. What belongs on a receiving note?","Station, physical bay, owner and seal together; the short label alone is ambiguous.","Ask the receiving custodian to repeat the location in their own words.","An owner’s collection instruction needs enough detail for the intended receiving desk to act on it."]],"arts":[["A voyage performance is popular because a crew’s private grief makes it moving. What would you ask?","Establish the source and permission for the particular account.","Ask the people represented how public use would affect them.","Popularity does not turn private testimony into unrestricted material."],["Two communities remember the same welcome differently. Must a performance choose one?","Keep the differences attributable rather than inventing a single official memory.","Make room for the quieter account as well as the familiar one.","People can decline to have their experience performed without denying another community’s account."],["A recording has been restored but not authenticated. How should it be introduced?","Describe the restoration separately from the unresolved provenance.","Let the audience understand whose voices have not been identified.","An uncertain recording can be heard with clear limits rather than sold as a verified personal history."]],"botany":[["A crop improvement depends on an input the station cannot currently obtain. What does a trial show?","Separate a successful trial from a sustainable production schedule.","Ask the growing crew which routine can survive the actual receiving delays.","A habitat may choose the experiment while retaining responsibility for its finite water and power."],["A visiting collector wants the whole living collection moved. What must be checked?","Identify containment, custody and the permission attached to each affected sample.","Hear the people who maintain the collection before calling it interchangeable sale stock.","One willing custodian cannot automatically consent for every steward or living subject."],["A failed trial has useful measurements but no harvest. Was it wasted?","Keep the observations and the conditions that produced them.","A grower should be able to report a failure without inventing a success to protect their standing.","The next trial is a fresh decision, with its resource cost and uncertainty visible."]],"teaching":[["A seasoned captain gives the right answer for a reason that no longer applies. What would you ask?","Use a changed example to distinguish remembered wording from current understanding.","Let experience remain valuable without making a correction humiliating.","A learner should be free to revise their explanation rather than defend every earlier answer."],["An apprentice sees an unsafe shortcut praised for saving time. What is the lesson?","Compare the missing check with the result, including what luck failed to reveal.","Ask whose later shift would carry the unreported risk.","An honest account of a repaired shortcut differs from falsely certifying that every check passed."],["A new arrival hears that a shared Compact means a single government. What would you clarify?","Name the political agreement, the separate drive agreement and the local authority.","Ask which part of the explanation created the confusion.","Shared rights and duties do not make every community or individual delegate interchangeable."]]};
const personalPlans={"help an apprentice open a business of their own":["They know the craft, but a tenancy agreement feels like a language designed to exclude them.","We sat together over a draft budget and marked which obligations still need an independent explanation.","Would you begin with the figures, the apprentice’s concerns, or their right to choose the risk?","independence"],"build a cooperative that shares emergency transport costs":["The crews with the least spare money are also the ones most exposed to a delayed rescue.","A few crews have agreed to compare the costs they actually faced before anyone promises a contribution.","How do we make the first agreement fair to crews whose emergencies are very different?","service"],"train an apprentice who will eventually disagree with me intelligently":["It is easy to teach someone to copy my checks and much harder to let them question my assumptions.","I asked the apprentice to explain a result I had accepted too quickly, and kept their objection in the teaching notes.","When their interpretation differs from mine, what should the next lesson protect first?","mentoring"],"bring a long-running neighborhood project to completion":["Everyone remembers the original promise differently, and nobody wants another impressive announcement.","We made a short list of unfinished pieces and asked the people still using the space which one mattered.","Who should decide what counts as a finished project?","community"],"finish a mechanical model that has occupied a corner of my cabin for years":["I can repair working machinery, but I keep redesigning this little model instead of finishing one moving part.","I assembled one small mechanism and left its first imperfect movement visible instead of taking it apart again.","Should I refine the measurements, ask someone to try it, or accept the version I actually enjoy?","craft"],"learn a difficult craft slowly enough to enjoy being a beginner":["Every professional habit tells me to hide the awkward first attempts.","I kept an unfinished practice piece and asked the teacher to show me one thing to change, not everything.","What would make it possible to keep learning without turning this into another test of competence?","mentoring"],"negotiate a fairer roster for people caring for family":["The quietest people on the roster are often the ones doing another shift of care after work.","We made room for people to describe the hours they could actually offer without publishing their family details.","How should a shared roster recognise a need someone cannot comfortably explain in public?","service"],"write a cookbook that explains why each substitution works":["A recipe from one habitat can fail completely with another station’s water and pantry.","I wrote down one substitution that failed, including what I had changed, instead of presenting only the successful meal.","Should the first reader see a precise trial, a cook’s experience, or room to adapt it themselves?","craft"],"restore an instrument that has outlived three stations":["A polished replacement would hide the repair marks that tell us how the instrument survived.","I catalogued one old repair before deciding which part could safely be worked on.","Which matters most when a useful object also carries a history?","archive"],"learn enough languages to stop relying on rushed translations":["I can memorise a formal phrase and still miss what a tired person means by it.","I asked a patient speaker to correct a short introduction and kept the explanation beside the words.","What should a first conversation in an unfamiliar language leave room for?","mentoring"],"leave a better maintenance archive than the one I inherited":["The old notes record what was replaced, but not why someone thought the replacement would help.","I rewrote one entry with the symptom, the operating conditions and the unanswered question together.","How do we make an archive useful without making its first author afraid to admit uncertainty?","archive"],"record an album with musicians who have never shared one room":["Every player hears a different delay, and a neat combined track can conceal who had to adapt.","We exchanged one short rehearsal and kept each player’s timing notes beside it.","Who should decide which differences belong in the recording?","creative"],"take a former mentor to the place described in all those old stories":["I have an affectionate version of those stories, but have not asked which place they would actually want to revisit.","I wrote a private invitation that asks what they would choose, rather than announcing a journey on their behalf.","What should an invitation like that promise?","reunion"],"build a small greenhouse that belongs to the whole shift":["A shared greenhouse can quietly become the project of whoever is most comfortable speaking at meetings.","The shift drew a small trial layout and left space for people to add the uses they wanted from it.","How should the first growing space be shared?","habitat"],"leave enough spare parts for the next person to improvise safely":["A shelf of miscellaneous parts is not the same as a reserve another person can identify and trust.","I began a local reference list that says which substitutions have actually been tested and which have not.","What should the next person know before improvising?","service"],"save enough to refuse the next dishonest contract":["It is easy to talk about refusing bad work while the next bill is still waiting.","I separated the obligations I have already accepted from the new work I can still decline.","What would make a reserve useful without letting its size become the only measure of a decent choice?","independence"],"finish a collection of ordinary people’s voyage stories":["The dramatic accounts arrive first; quiet routines are harder to persuade people are worth recording.","I made a place for one modest account and asked its speaker how it should be attributed.","Who should control the way an ordinary life is presented to strangers?","archive"],"make the station’s emergency instructions understandable without a specialist":["A technically correct instruction can still leave a frightened newcomer unsure which door to use.","We tested one draft instruction by asking a new arrival to explain the first action in their own words.","What should we change when a reader follows the words but misses the intended action?","service"],"fund a small traveling exhibition of ordinary station life":["The exhibition needs permission as well as transport, and I do not want generosity to hide either obligation.","I prepared a small proposal naming the contributors and the permissions still outstanding.","How should the contributors shape what travels?","creative"],"complete a guide to repairing the equipment smaller stations cannot replace":["A repair that works in a well-stocked workshop can be a dangerous instruction at a station missing the same tools.","I added the required tools and stopping conditions to one draft repair, not just its successful sequence.","Which limitation should a repair guide make hardest to overlook?","craft"],"make the station’s first-job training kinder and more practical":["New hands can learn very quickly which questions make a supervisor impatient.","I asked a learner to mark the point where the induction stopped making sense, and kept that mark in the draft.","How should we respond when a first-job learner exposes a gap in the lesson?","mentoring"],"learn how to sail on an actual sea":["I know how to read an orbital plan, but that does not make me a sailor.","I found an introductory lesson and wrote down the questions I would rather ask before reaching the water.","How would you approach being an inexperienced traveller in a place everyone assumes you understand?","journey"],"help a scattered family meet at one table again":["One person’s happy reunion can become another person’s unwanted obligation.","I sent a question about what people would welcome, with room to say no without giving a reason.","What should be settled before anyone books passage?","reunion"],"turn a temporary residence into a home worth returning to":["It is possible to keep improving a room without letting another person feel welcome in it.","I made room for one ordinary habit that belongs here, rather than arranging everything for my next departure.","What makes a place feel chosen rather than merely occupied?","community"],"restore a family heirloom without erasing the marks of its repairs":["The worn surface includes the work of people whose names never reached a formal record.","I documented one old join before attempting a reversible cleaning test.","What should restoration preserve when a clean finish would tell a simpler story?","archive"],"teach a class where no one feels embarrassed to ask a basic question":["A room can be friendly in its opening speech and impatient at the first interruption.","We tried a short lesson where a learner could stop the explanation without having to justify the question.","What should the teacher do with an interruption that reveals a mistaken assumption?","mentoring"],"make room for someone who has not yet found where they belong":["It is tempting to decide what another person needs before asking whether they want company.","I began with an invitation that offered a quiet place as well as a shared table.","How can an invitation leave the recipient genuinely free to choose?","community"],"take a year to visit the people I usually only hear over a radio":["I have imagined a route, but the people at its stops have lives that do not wait for my timetable.","I began a list of questions and invitations instead of a schedule of promised reunions.","Whose timetable should shape the first visit?","journey"],"open an archive where workers can record problems without fear of blame":["A promise of openness is not enough if a name can be used against the person who reports a fault.","I drafted separate handling rules for a technical observation and the identity of its contributor.","What should a useful archive protect when evidence and privacy pull in different directions?","archive"],"finish a project without taking it home every night":["I am very good at treating one more revision as a reason never to stop.","I chose one small piece to finish during a shift and left the rest of its questions on the workbench.","Who should decide when a good enough piece of work is allowed to stay finished?","craft"],"reunite the surviving members of a long-retired survey crew":["The old crew may remember the same voyage in ways that no reunion can tidy into one account.","I prepared an invitation that asks what each person would like to share, or keep private.","What should a reunion leave unresolved rather than force into a single story?","reunion"],"organize a festival that every shift can attend":["A festival at one convenient hour is only for the shift that happens to be free.","We compared overlapping small gatherings with one large event before announcing a date.","What would make the gathering belong to the whole station?","creative"],"put together a reliable emergency supply cooperative":["Everyone agrees about helping until the first argument about who pays and who receives the reserve.","A few volunteers listed the needs they could actually document and the responsibilities they could accept.","How should the first reserve be governed?","service"],"start a shared workshop with no membership fee":["Removing a fee does not answer who gets the scarce bench time or keeps the tools in working order.","We drafted a small shared-use rota with an explicit way to report a damaged tool.","What should happen when access for one person makes the next person’s work harder?","community"],"plan a journey for pleasure instead of a deadline":["I keep turning a pleasant idea into an efficient list of things to accomplish.","I left one unassigned stop in a draft route and asked what I would enjoy even if nothing useful came of it.","What should remain open in a journey chosen for its own sake?","journey"],"pay back a kindness that cannot be measured in credits":["A gift can become uncomfortable when its recipient is told what repayment should look like.","I wrote a note explaining what the kindness made possible, without attaching an obligation to answer.","How can gratitude avoid becoming another demand?","reunion"],"design a habitat garden that needs very little imported water":["A convincing garden drawing is not yet a measured water budget or a place residents want to spend time.","We prepared a small, documented trial plan and asked residents which uses mattered to them.","How should a scarce water allowance shape a shared garden?","habitat"],"make an accessible instrument for a friend who misses playing":["I can build what I think would help and still miss the way my friend wants to make music.","I asked which movement and sound they wanted to try before choosing a mechanism.","Who should lead the next design decision?","creative"],"build a recording archive before old voices disappear":["Urgency can make a request to record someone feel like an obligation they never chose.","I prepared a simple permission record with choices about attribution, access and withdrawal before recording.","What should be protected when there may not be another chance to ask?","archive"],"give the next generation a less precarious first job":["Advice is easy to offer; a learner also needs someone to explain the obligation before they sign it.","I began a first-job checklist with a place to ask for independent help.","How should we recognise that a new hand may not feel free to challenge the person hiring them?","mentoring"],"restore the old public observation gallery":["A restored window is not much of a public space if only one shift has a chance to use it.","The first proposal separates the repair questions from the opening hours people have asked for.","What should the gallery’s first reopening make room for?","community"],"build a quiet room that anyone between contracts can use":["A welcoming room still needs rules that do not make a visitor explain why they need quiet.","We drafted a simple arrangement for shared use and a private way to raise a concern.","How should the room protect both access and peace?","community"],"make a useful invention simple enough for anyone to repair":["A clever assembly can hide its simplest fault behind a part only its maker understands.","I drew one mechanism with the failure points and replaceable interfaces visible.","What should I simplify before asking someone else to depend on it?","craft"],"open a quiet reading room beside the busiest corridor":["The very place that makes the room easy to find also brings noise and competing uses.","I asked the people on different shifts where a quieter entrance and clear opening hours would help.","Who should shape the rules of a room meant to welcome strangers?","community"]};
const personalOutcomes={"mentoring":["We kept the learner’s original question beside the corrected explanation. It can now challenge the next lesson instead of disappearing from it.","We began with the learner’s own account of where the explanation failed. The next small lesson follows that point.","We left the learner room to choose the next attempt and say when the explanation had stopped making sense."],"archive":["We kept the original source and the limits of its permission beside the new record.","We asked the contributors how the record should represent them before deciding its final form.","We recorded the contributor’s choices about use and attribution without claiming that one permission covered everything."],"community":["We made the shared arrangement explicit enough that the next shift can question it.","We began by hearing people who had not spoken in the first meeting. The arrangement changed because of their answer.","We kept participation voluntary and left a clear way to change the arrangement later."],"creative":["We kept the trial and its permissions beside the work, rather than presenting the result as if nobody had made choices.","We asked the people contributing the work what they wanted the receiving audience to understand.","We left the contributors control over what they wished to share. That changed the shape of the first small piece."],"craft":["We kept the working measurements and the unresolved limit together. One small piece can now be left finished honestly.","We asked someone else to try the small piece before deciding what to revise. Their experience changed the next step.","We chose a version whose limits I could explain and left room for the next person to adapt it."],"reunion":["I kept the invitation clear about what had been offered and what had not been promised.","I asked what the other people would welcome before treating my hope as a shared plan.","The invitation leaves room to decline or choose a different kind of contact. That makes it a real invitation."],"habitat":["We kept the measured limits and the proposed uses together, rather than declaring a successful garden from a drawing.","The people on different shifts added uses the first plan had overlooked. The trial proposal changed.","We left the residents a meaningful choice within the stated resource limits. A shared garden needs more than a caretaker’s enthusiasm."],"service":["We wrote down who could accept each responsibility and which need was actually documented.","We began with the people who would rely on the arrangement. Their account changed what the first small promise should be.","We made the limits clear and left the affected people room to choose the help they could accept."],"independence":["I separated the known obligations from the assumptions in the first plan. That gives the next decision a clearer footing.","We began by hearing which part of the risk the person taking it was most concerned about.","We left the final choice with the person who would live with it, after explaining the obligations plainly."],"journey":["I kept the practical limits visible without filling every part of the journey with another obligation.","I asked the people at the receiving end what sort of visit they would welcome. The first plan changed.","I left a real choice about the route and the welcome, including room for a person to say that this was not the right time."]};
